# app-close-home: menu-hygiene decisions 5 and 6.
#
# Decision 5: `{"cmd":"app","text":"off"}` really closes RTTY. RTTY is not a
# dialog, so `main_screen_close_app()` (the function the remote control calls,
# src/remote_server.cpp -> open_app()) has to close it too, and the button bar
# has to go back to the page it had before the app opened.
#
# Decision 6: closing a dialog goes back to the bar's pre-open state, not to the
# "stuck" page of the previous app. The repro (#50): open RTTY, then a dialog ->
# on close the bar stayed on RTTY's page instead of the home page.
#
# The route is the firmware's own: scenario_build opens RTTY with
# main_screen_start_app(ACTION_APP_RTTY); scenario_settle closes it with
# main_screen_close_app(), then opens RTTY again, opens the real Ajustes window
# over it (main_screen_action(ACTION_APP_SETTINGS)) and closes the dialog.
# scenario_settle codifies both checkpoints (RTTY off, bar back on the home page)
# and stops the run instead of capturing a green screen if they do not hold.
#
# The radio state matches home-usb-20m so the only difference is the route and
# the bar it leaves behind.

name app-close-home
screen app-close-home

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
